Experimental source-owned settings persistence retirement; not applied by Context Foundry.
Target: can1357/oh-my-pi @ 24439066040e006eb08da7b204f0ac41c79d2de9
Owner: 003 T006, bounded-pilot-v2 startup observation and admission.
Requires the existing caller/auth/refusal/restricted patches and
omp-startup-discovery-retirement.patch.
Modules: Settings::retireStartupPersistence, concrete reload/save callers;
main::Settings.init, sdk::retireRestrictedStartupSettings.
Tests: startup-settings-owner.test.ts; existing settings/auth/restricted SDK suites.
Difference: one opt-in persistence owner established at Settings construction.
It closes public mutations/reloads and watching, joins the original admitted reloads,
rescopes, saves and completion observers, preserves staged writes, then cancels timers.
Original CLI auth/settings link retirement precedes this drain. No second session
link is created when the CLI supplies both authStorage and modelRegistry.
The restricted owner refuses derived settings clones/overlays; ordinary use is unchanged.
At most 4096 operation starts. Bind to the exact already sealed session/registry/settings.
No auth-store physical descriptor close, general OAuth drain, complete startup inventory,
Ready, transport permission, paid execution or release signing is established.

